      "title": "Samsung-led partners plan licensing for nuclear-powered LNG carrier",
      "content_html": "Samsung Heavy Industries, U.S. reactor developer Tesser Atomics, the Norwegian University of Science and Technology (NTNU) and classification society DNV agreed to develop a nuclear safety, licensing and approval plan for a proposed nuclear-powered LNG carrier. The concept uses Tesser’s marine fluoride-salt-cooled reactor and is intended as a demonstration project within Norway’s SFI SAINT nuclear-vessel research centre.\n\nThe work covers reactor development and licensing, hazard identification, safety assessment and maritime classification; the partners also plan feasibility studies, modelling and testing. Tesser CEO Per Peterson said the Norwegian research consortium had accelerated work on legal, regulatory and insurance questions. The project remains at the concept stage, with safety assessments and an approval roadmap among the next tasks.",
